{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310634,"nonce":"lVF0Siw4IZTiRvKxBMDiRMxCtLg=","title":"Cross-file interface method dispatch silently elided — FIXED (a86d8a9) by plumbing interface metadata across files + cross-file vtable ...","message":"`tok.vocabSize()` where `tok:Tokenizer` (interface) used to silently drop the call AND the entire surrounding expression (string concat, trace call) because `lower_expression` returned `None` from a failed dispatch and the None cascaded through the format chain.\n\n**Root cause (3 distinct gaps).** Fixed in `a86d8a9` (`fix(hir_to_mir): plumb interface metadata + cross-file vtable resolution + return wrap`):\n\n1. **Interface metadata was per-file.** `interface_method_names`, `interface_method_return_types`, `interface_extends`, and `interface_vtables` lived on `HirToMirContext` and were never shared across compilation units. Main.hx referencing `Tokenizer` declared in `nue/tokenizer/Tokenizer.hx` started with empty maps → dispatch lookup returned None.\n\n2. **`wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr` looked up methods in the wrong map.** It only consulted per-context `function_map`, missing cross-file methods. Vtable slots ended up zero-filled → calling them jumped to address 0.\n\n3. **`Return` of a class value when the function returns an interface didn't wrap.** `lower_expression`'s auto-wrap fires only when `expr.ty` is interface; for `return classInstance` the expression type stays as the class. The caller dispatched through a raw class pointer treated as a fat pointer.\n\n**Fix anatomy:**\n- Added `interface_method_names`, `interface_method_return_types`, `interface_extends`, `interface_vtables` to `MirLoweringResult` and as parameters to `lower_hir_to_mir_with_function_map`.\n- Added matching `import_interface_*` accumulators on `CompilationUnit`; merge them after each lowering.\n- `wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr`: also consult `external_function_map` when method symbol isn't in local `function_map`.\n- `HirStatement::Return`: call `maybe_wrap_for_interface(val, e.ty, fn_ret_ty)` before returning. Mirrors the wrap at Let and Assign sites.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- If a user reports \"trace doesn't print\" when an interface-typed receiver is involved, this fix already handles it.\n- Any new code path that produces a class value but is assigned/returned/passed where an interface is expected must go through `maybe_wrap_for_interface` (Let, Assign, and Return are now covered; call args are handled by the auto-wrap in `lower_expression`).\n\n**Remaining downstream blocker for llama-smoke (2026-05-23).** Past the interface fix, `GGUFTokenizer.build` now enters and runs through token vocab population. Stops silently between iter 1 and 100 of `for (m in mergeStrings) { parseMerge(m) }`. Symptom: exit 0 with no error message, but no completion trace either. NOT an interface issue. Likely candidates: `String.substr` / `String.indexOf` edge case on UTF-8 multi-byte chars (`Ġ` is U+0120, two bytes), `Array.push` on large arrays, or a different elision somewhere in `parseMerge`. Separate work cycle.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_interface_dispatch_elision` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}